# GitHub language statistics.
#
# `legacy-python/` is the original Python implementation, kept in the tree as a
# reference for the Rust port (and deliberately excluded by
# `src/analyzer/walker.rs`). GitHub otherwise counts those 440K as this
# repository's primary language and labels the whole project "Python".
# Marking it vendored keeps it readable in the tree while removing it from the
# language breakdown, so the repo reads as what it is: a Rust crate.
legacy-python/** linguist-vendored

# Derived/generated files — keep them out of the language stats.
Cargo.lock linguist-generated
